2884,-2.062299427052494e-05,-1.156323378381785e-05,-0.0004895919119007885,0.0,-0.00016056202002801,0.0,0.0,-0.01256337109953165,-0.0005417786305770278,-4.768370445162873e-07,-0.0062752352096140385,-1.0728830375228426e-06,-1.1801649634435307e-05,-9.536738616588991e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.0012075759004801512,-6.01988795096986e-05,0.0,-7.867782187531702e-06,-2.7418097943154862e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,46254,510,59,9640,59,15940,1124,37018,35702,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,18,59,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,20,59,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,22,59,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,24,59,2493,15170,16,17,92,488,1124,15940,1124,37018,90,16,16,59,2493,15170,16,17,27275,59,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nCompute:\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{9\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{12}.\n\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"8bc3dd5d0b7fe41a1256a3e1e2b4a4097eafaa07177862198427d53a22408845"},"seconds":63.263572692871094,"seed":536598179670325727,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the given problem, we will compute the sum of the sine values step by step. The expression is:\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{9\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{12}.\n\\]\n\nFirst, we simplify the arguments of the sine functions:\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{12}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the identity \\(\\sin(\\pi - x) = \\sin x\\) to simplify some of the terms:\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{11\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\left(\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right) = \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{7\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\left(\\pi - \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right) = \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{4} = \\sin \\left(\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12}.\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\\[\n2 \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + 2 \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2 \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12}.\n\\]\n\nFactoring out the 2, we have:\n\\[\n2 \\left( \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right).\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the values of \\(\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12}\\), \\(\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\), and \\(\\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\):\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\left(15^\\circ\\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = \\sin \\left(75^\\circ\\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} + \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n\\]\n\nCombining the fractions:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{4} + \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2} + 2\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{6} + 2\\sqrt{2}}{4} = \\frac{2(\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2})}{4} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n2 \\left( \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right) = \\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
